    "media:imagetext": "ASPEN AIRWAYS, INC.\nCV-580\nThe airplane on which you are traveling is one of\nthe safest aircraft in service today. Your safety is\nalways our first concern, and our pilots and flight\nattendants are thoroughly trained to cope with\nany emergency which might arise. Should it be necessary to evacuate the aircraft,\nthere are a number of exits available for your use. These are described below.\nFRONT\nWINDOW\nEXITS\nREAR\nENTRANCE 41\nShall not be used as\nan exit unless directed by a crew member\nDOOR\nWITH\nEXIT\nSLIDE\nWINDOW EXITS\nGrasp handle inside\nslot over window.\nPull in and down.\nLift window. Turn on\nside and throw out.\nFace rear of cabin.\nIf over wing, step out,\nsit down on rear of wing\nand slide to ground.\nIf not over wing, pull\nescape rope from top of\nwindow trame, climb out\nwindow feet first, climb\nor slide to ground.\nREAR DOOR EXIT\nOPEN\nTurn handle to the\nrear and up.\nPush door out to open.\nPull red handle to\ninflate slide.\nMove away from aircraft quickly\n(OVER)\nRemove high heel\nshoes-jump onto\nslide with feet up.",
